  "worked_solution": "First, as $x\\to -\\infty ,$ we can assume that $x<-4.$ So, we use the following expression for $f(x):$\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{2}+3x\n$$\n\nNow, we identify the leading term and compute its limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }({x}^{2}+3x) & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }({x}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\infty \\end{aligned}\n$$",
